{
 "id": "2026-10-09-second-front",
 "lang": "en",
 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "rate": 6.7,
   "text": "The Iran war just opened a second front. And your heating bill is the target."
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "In July, Saudi Arabia asked Trump for permission to restart its war on Yemen. According to Axios, he said yes. Now Pakistan, Turkey and Syria are backing Riyadh, and the US is reportedly providing intelligence and refueling Saudi jets."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "Yemen's Houthis hit back with a Red Sea blockade of Saudi Arabia. That's exactly where Saudi oil escaped after Iran closed Hormuz. Now both exits are choked: Hormuz carries about 20 percent of the world's traded oil, Bab al-Mandab about 8. The IEA calls it the biggest oil supply crisis in history."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "The result? Crude is back above 100 dollars. Shipping an oil tanker to East Asia now costs 1.3 million dollars a day, up from 60,000. And heating oil in Maine is up 80 percent."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Follow for the next update."
  }
 ],
